            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "A thickness problem is gummy and patchy, following low spots, overlaps and areas worked twice. A cold failure is chalky or powdery and fairly uniform across the whole patio, and may rub off as dust rather than sticky residue. Moisture problems often show white blushing alongside the tackiness."
          }
